# TD GAMES BILLING — Multi-Module Platform (Invoice + Expense)

Restructure the existing Invoice app into a multi-module **TD GAMES BILLING** platform. Add a new **Expense** module for cost tracking alongside the existing **Invoice** module for revenue tracking.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Architecture Decision: Module Switcher vs Router**
> I propose a **top-level module switcher** (dropdown/tabs in Navbar) instead of adding a full React Router. This keeps the app lightweight and avoids a major refactor. The Navbar will have an "Invoice" | "Expense" toggle at the top, and each module will have its own internal tabs.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Client Data Sharing**
> Both modules share the same NocoDB `Thông tin khách hàng` table. Changes to client info in either module will be reflected in both. No duplication needed.

> [!WARNING]
> **Scope Clarification**
> The Dashboard module (Revenue vs Expense overview) will be built later as a separate 3rd module per user's request. This plan only covers Invoice + Expense.

---

## Proposed Changes

### App Shell — Module Navigation

#### [MODIFY] [Navbar.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/Navbar.tsx)
- Add a **module switcher** (styled dropdown/tabs) near the logo: `📄 Invoice` | `💰 Expense`
- Each module has its own set of internal tabs
- Invoice tabs: `edit`, `preview`, `history`, `dashboard`, `activity`, `recurring`
- Expense tabs: `expenses`, `categories`, `recurring`, `activity`

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/App.tsx)
- Add `activeModule` state: `'invoice' | 'expense'`
- Conditionally render Invoice module or Expense module based on `activeModule`
- Keep all existing Invoice logic intact (zero changes to Invoice behavior)

#### [MODIFY] [types.ts](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/types.ts)
- Add Expense-related types: `ExpenseRecord`, `ExpenseCategory`, `Vendor`, `RecurringExpense`

---

### Expense Module — Components

#### [NEW] [ExpenseApp.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/expense/ExpenseApp.tsx)
- Main container for the Expense module (analogous to the Invoice editor flow in App.tsx)
- Manages its own internal tab state: expenses list, add/edit expense, categories, recurring

#### [NEW] [ExpenseList.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/expense/ExpenseList.tsx)
- Table view of all expenses with sorting and filtering
- Filters: category, project, client, date range, status
- Quick stats: total this month, by category breakdown

#### [NEW] [ExpenseForm.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/expense/ExpenseForm.tsx)
- Add/Edit expense form with fields:
  - Description, Amount, Currency (USD/VND), Date
  - Category (dropdown from categories table)
  - Project, Client (synced from shared client table)
  - Payment method, Vendor/Payee
  - Notes, Attachments (receipt images)
  - Is Recurring toggle → frequency settings

#### [NEW] [ExpenseCategoryManager.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/expense/ExpenseCategoryManager.tsx)
- CRUD for expense categories with color coding
- Default categories: Freelancer, Tool/License, Server Hosting, Tax, Salary, Equipment, Office Rent

#### [NEW] [ExpenseRecurring.tsx](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/components/expense/ExpenseRecurring.tsx)
- Manage recurring expenses (monthly server fees, salaries, rent, etc.)
- Show next due date, auto-generate reminders

---

### Expense Module — Data Layer

#### [NEW] [expenseService.ts](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/services/expenseService.ts)
- NocoDB CRUD operations for expense records
- Uses existing `TDC_Finace` base (id: `p95wenplq8hbmjr`)
- Will create new NocoDB tables:
  - `Expenses` — main expense records
  - `Expense Categories` — category management
  - `Expense_Recurring` — recurring expense templates

#### [NEW] [useExpenseState.ts](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/hooks/useExpenseState.ts)
- Similar pattern to [useInvoiceState.ts](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/td-games-invoice-app/hooks/useInvoiceState.ts)
- Manages expense list, filters, categories, form state, CRUD operations

---

### NocoDB Tables (TDC_Finace base)

**Expenses table:**
| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| Title | SingleLineText | Expense description |
| Amount | Decimal | Expense amount |
| Currency | SingleSelect | USD, VND |
| Date | Date | Expense date |
| Category | SingleSelect | Linked categories |
| Project | SingleLineText | Project name |
| Client | SingleLineText | Client name (synced) |
| Vendor | SingleLineText | Who was paid |
| Payment Method | SingleSelect | Cash, Bank Transfer, Card, Other |
| Status | SingleSelect | Pending, Approved, Paid |
| Notes | LongText | Additional notes |
| Receipt | Attachment | Receipt images |
| Is Recurring | Checkbox | Recurring flag |
| Recurring Frequency | SingleSelect | Monthly, Quarterly, Yearly |
| Created By | SingleLineText | User who created |
| Created At | DateTime | Auto timestamp |

---

## Verification Plan

### Browser Testing
1. Start server with `npm run dev`
2. Navigate to `http://localhost:3000`
3. Verify module switcher appears in Navbar (Invoice / Expense toggle)
4. Switch to Expense module → verify Expense UI loads
5. Switch back to Invoice → verify all Invoice functionality still works unchanged
6. Add a new expense record in Expense module
7. Verify category management CRUD
8. Verify client dropdown shows shared client data

### Manual Verification
- User confirms the module switcher UX is intuitive
- User tests adding real expense data
- User verifies client data appears in both modules
